# LLM provider config. Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in ONE of the blocks
# below. The model CLIs (assess/eval) auto-load .env from the repo root;
# `npm run serve` / `npm run explorer` also load .env from their working directory.
# Exported variables take precedence; Settings can store a key server-side.
#
# NOTHING here is needed for the free path: `npm run scan -- --dir <ext>` is
# static-only — no key, no network, no spend.
#
# Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint works (base URL + API key); the presets below
# are that one shape pre-filled. The same values drive EVERY arm — pi (the
# default) as well as monolith / dag / the claim-verifier.

# --- preset: Ollama Cloud (default when OLLAMA_API_KEY is set) ---
# Create a key at https://ollama.com/settings/keys
OLLAMA_API_KEY=
# Optional: override the Ollama host (default https://ollama.com)
# OLLAMA_HOST=https://ollama.com

# --- preset: OpenAI ---
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# --- preset: NVIDIA NIM (hosted free endpoints for prototyping) ---
# Create a key at https://build.nvidia.com/ and choose a model with a Free Endpoint.
# EXTRAY_LLM_PROVIDER=nvidia
# NVIDIA_API_KEY=
# Optional: override the endpoint (default https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1)
# NVIDIA_BASE_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1
# Set SCORECARD_MODEL below to the exact NVIDIA catalog ID, without an Ollama
# :cloud suffix. Example (not evaluated on our corpus):
# SCORECARD_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning-30b-a3b
# Free endpoint availability and rate limits vary; see docs/configuration.md.

# --- preset: any other OpenAI-compatible endpoint (vLLM, LM Studio, llama.cpp,
# --- OpenRouter, Groq, Together, a local Ollama). Point at the /v1 root; the key
# --- is optional for a local server that needs no auth.
# EXTRAY_LLM_PROVIDER=openai-compatible
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# These override any preset, whichever one is selected:
# EXTRAY_LLM_PROVIDER=ollama|openai|nvidia|openai-compatible
# EXTRAY_LLM_BASE_URL=
# EXTRAY_LLM_API_KEY=

# Escape hatch for a CUSTOM adapter (a module default-exporting an LlmClient).
# It wins over every preset above; leave it unset unless you wrote one.
# LLM_ADAPTER=src/llm/providers/ollama-cloud.ts

# Default models (overridable per-run with --model / --model2). Pass the exact
# provider model id. The pilot's second rater MUST be a different model family.
#
# MODEL CHOICE IS A CORRECTNESS VARIABLE, not a cost variable — see
# src/llm/model-table.ts. Measured: glm-5.2 (and qwen3.5, which is no longer
# served on Ollama Cloud) classify the disclosure-gap case correctly; gemma4 regresses it to "analytics"; minimax-m3
# produced literally nothing; kimi-k2.7 thrashed to the turn ceiling. The CLIs
# warn on anything not measured-good.
#
# OFFLINE EVAL REPLAY: `npm run eval` replays committed fixtures with no API key,
# but ONLY for exactly this config (replay is exact-match on model + prompt):
#   --methodology monolith --model glm-5.2:cloud --think high \
#   --verifier-model gpt-oss:120b --judge-model gpt-oss:120b
# Setting SCORECARD_MODEL to anything else (or changing think/verifier/judge)
# leaves no fixtures to replay: you need a live RECORD run (key required, costs
# money). Pass the flags above explicitly rather than relying on .env.
SCORECARD_MODEL=glm-5.2:cloud
# The judge/normalizer model MUST be a different model family than the arm it
# grades (self-grading is leniency-biased; the CLI warns when they match).
# SCORECARD_JUDGE_MODEL=<a-different-model-family>
# The claim-verifier model SHOULD also be a different family than the arm
# (self-verification measured ~77% confirm-rate leniency; the CLI warns when
# they match). Changing it re-keys every verify-claim fixture — pair the switch
# with a RECORD run. The committed eval fixtures were recorded with
# gpt-oss:120b as verifier (and judge); minimax-m3 is now a measured-poor arm.
# SCORECARD_VERIFIER_MODEL=gpt-oss:120b
PILOT_MODEL=glm-5.2:cloud
# PILOT_MODEL2=<a-different-model-family>

# Host-enrichment (improvement 015) RDAP lookups touch the network ONLY in the
# enrich-hosts CLI (RECORD); the pipeline/report only read the committed
# artifact, so NO key is required. Optional: per-attempt RDAP fetch timeout in ms
# (default 15000) — widen for slow RIR/registry RDAP servers on a RECORD run.
# HOST_ENRICHMENT_TIMEOUT_MS=15000

# Model reasoning effort for the monolith assessment, mapped to Ollama's `think`
# field (overridable per-run with --think). Accepts: true, false, or a graded
# level low|medium|high on models that support it (e.g. gpt-oss). Leave unset to
# omit the knob entirely — changing it changes model output, so it is part of the
# fixture key and needs a fresh RECORD run.
# SCORECARD_THINK=high
